#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build the playable Zeboim Mass Driver dungeon for Xenogears Disc 2.

This standalone build clones thirty-three coherent retail fields into audited
unused Disc 2 slots and rewires them into a complete story dungeon.  A
working two-field Zeboim inclined lift completes its native descent at the
authored lower landing before opening into two car-free Lighthouse transit
tunnels and an abandoned employee subway terminus.  A service vestibule,
Repair Bot merchant, pressure-transfer airlock, every internal room, and both
interlocking wings, a three-door archive branch, and nine reciprocal archive
annexes come from retail
Xenogears resources; the facility route
after the platform uses the actual Disc 1 Ethos Dig Site / Zeboim ruins where
Emeralda is found, and there is no train ride.  Research records reveal a
five-entry launch authorization, visible controls restore the dormant rail,
and Vierge and Crescens wait together beyond a new archive lift inside a
large below-grade Goliath Factory hall. Approaching the adjacent Gears starts
one boarding scene and the surviving Zeboim security-machine battle.
Five containment vaults reconstructed from cleaned retail field-673 geometry
then lead directly to the Mass Driver's Zeboim Central Control room, where the
complete finale plays.
Citan appears there for the first time at an authentic compact standing keypad
imported from the retail Zeboim access tunnel and placed on Elly's newest
captured east-wall marker, opposite her wall computer bank. A separate hidden
contact actor makes the relocated fixture physically solid, while its small
front reader lets Elly remark that it looks out of place before the finale.
He visibly operates it while
the party commits Taura's
nanomachine capsule instead of a nuclear payload.  A one-time New
Game bootstrap stages Elly and Emeralda, opens the playable world map outside
the facility, and never enters the retail Disc 2 story director.

The dungeon is a canon-conscious fan reconstruction, not recovered Square
script or cut-content data.
"""

